  "2026-10-19T15:20:37.601Z",codex-agent,"Verified implementation commit 7a83d9532253b760782f3b6ac13132d6a566dfbf from separate no-local clones with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config. npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass: 1349 tests, 1347 pass, 2 existing opt-in real-data fleet skips, 0 fail/cancel/TODO. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 across all 30 measured source files at unchanged per-file thresholds. Duplication is 0 percent across 27319 measured lines; 251 declarations pass the docstring gate; production audit has zero vulnerabilities. Package dry-run, changelog/date, canonical publish-attestation and lifecycle gates all pass. GitHub Node 22/26, Windows consumers 22/26 and CodeQL also pass on this commit. Fresh-clone strict health passes after normal pinned SDK setup, with only the existing stale-item advisory. PM-linked commands pass 19/19 plus 1/1; result storage is disabled, so this comment preserves the receipt. Packed npm/Node/npx and native Bun/bunx candidate consumers pass actual package activation, strict tracker health and the release-caller policy. actionlint v1.7.12 passes with only its documented job.workflow_sha property gap ignored; every shell block passes bash -n. No threshold or auditor exclusion was added. No PM CLI/SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-19T15:20:39.640Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/183. Inventory is 28 readable byte-distinct workflows and 713 classified structural deltas (123 cosmetic/stale, 318 package needs, 272 defects). Both migration callers pass structure/input-name validation after replacing the deliberate zero-SHA marker. All 22 typed inputs are documented. pm-github 152 is merged and its fetched main workflow is byte-identical to the ported head. Remaining work is the approved release/pilot/migration and the two inventory gaps in ops-release-inventory-gaps. Live publishing is not certified by local gates; neutral/skipped review services are not approvals. No consumer source, hosted setting, software tag or release was changed. Leaving this item in progress for orchestrator verification and closeout; releasing the claim now."
  "2026-10-19T15:23:46.630Z",codex-agent,"Final migration review found a required upstream coupling: the canonical attestation auditor rejects a thin caller because it contains no local publish command. Reclaimed this item to add explicit recognition of the exact SHA-pinned pm-ops caller, with regressions proving that foreign refs, private jobs and adjacent unattested publish paths still fail. The already-passing 7a83d95 receipts remain historical implementation evidence; the final implementation will be re-gated."
  "2026-10-19T15:34:10.025Z",codex-agent,"Caller migration coupling is now handled upstream: the canonical auditor recognizes only the structurally valid, SHA-pinned pm-ops release.yml caller and reports an explicit upstream delegation. It still audits every adjacent local, foreign or unresolved publisher and preserves malformed-source failures. New regressions pass 3/3; reverting only canonicalReleaseDelegation to the old unrecognized behavior fails all 3 (0 pass). A real tracked Git fixture proves a caller-only consumer passes and an added unguarded package script fails. All focused tests pass 23/23. Migration docs require the one-time automated Dependabot pm-ops upgrade and conversion of old local-workflow shape guards before the caller wave; no consumers were edited."
  "2026-10-19T15:48:31.721Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation verification: 89fb4d75d80fba52a0a58c598984b9c783209a8e passes npm run release:check and bun run release:check in independent no-local clones with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Each run reports 1352 tests: 1350 pass, 2 existing opt-in real-data fleet skips, 0 fail/cancel/TODO. Coverage is 100/100/100/100 across all 30 measured source files at unchanged per-file thresholds. Duplication is 0 percent across 27391 measured lines; 251 declarations pass docstrings; production audit finds zero vulnerabilities. Typecheck, lint, package dry-run, changelog/date, canonical attestation of both release workflows, and lifecycle gates all pass. Normal pinned merge setup followed by fresh-clone strict health passes with the existing stale-item advisory. PM-linked commands pass 19/19, 1/1 and 3/3; result storage is disabled, so this comment preserves the receipt. Packed npm/Node/npx and native Bun/bunx consumers pass real package activation, strict tracker health, caller policy and delegated attestation. Pure-function control passes 10/10; selection, ownership and daily-cap behavioral reversions each fail 2 tests. Delegation control passes 3/3; reverting only recognition fails all 3. actionlint v1.7.12 passes with only its documented job.workflow_sha diagnostic gap ignored; parsed tests run bash -n for every shell block. No threshold or publisher-audit exclusion was added. No PM CLI/SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-19T15:48:33.823Z",codex-agent,"Final handoff: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/183. The upstream recheck confirms pm-github 152 merged and fetched main 5f169971d4a5f37d48795512c2c100ccf571c8d9 has a byte-identical release workflow to the ported head. Inventory: 28 readable workflows with 28 distinct MD5s; 713 structural deltas classified as 123 cosmetic/stale, 318 legitimate package needs and 272 defects. All 22 typed inputs and exact pm-csv/Rust migration callers are documented. The migration requires the first approved released workflow SHA, automated pm-ops dependency upgrades, and conversion of existing private workflow-shape guards to caller checks. Live trusted publishing and controlled pilots remain unverified. Required CI jobs on the final implementation are still queued; neutral, skipped and unavailable review services are not approvals. The two inventory gaps remain open in ops-release-inventory-gaps. No consumer source, hosted setting, software tag or release was changed. Releasing the claim while leaving this item in progress for orchestrator verification and closeout."
  "2026-10-19T16:48:30.739Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 at c81f0fc: verified all five unresolved CodeRabbit findings and read all review bodies; no additional outside-diff findings. Plan: canonical release-tag provenance via shipped metadata and explicit online refresh, caller issues-write grants, parsed nested-permission union regression, and documented Bun test prerequisites. Existing workflow self-version resolver already reads canonical tags and rejects untagged commits; add fork-only boundary proof. No review replies or resolutions, merge, or release."
  "2026-10-19T16:51:29.071Z",codex-agent,"Six isolated behavioral reverts each failed their focused regression (0 pass, 1 fail, zero skips): canonical tag binding, required issues-write policy, template issues-write grant, weakened conditional alert grant for the permission-union test, Bun prerequisite documentation, and removal of the pre-existing workflow missing-tag refusal. Sources restored after every proof. Canonical snapshot contains 54 release tags fetched from the canonical GitHub refs API. Annotated/nested tag peeling, cycles, malformed objects, API failure, fork-only pins and decoy YAML comments are covered."
  "2026-10-19T16:56:10.680Z",codex-agent,"Focused regressions pass 19/19; all four PM-linked commands pass (24, 2, 3, and 19 assertions respectively). Independent focused c8 reports 100% statements/branches/functions/lines for release-caller.ts and scripts/release-caller.ts. Live canonical API refresh byte-matches the 54-tag shipped snapshot; compiled dist accepts the canonical pin and rejects the fork-only fixture. Isolated pinned-tooling strict PM health passes with only the existing stale-item advisory. Offline snapshots cannot name their own future release commit: documentation requires a later snapshot-bearing package for offline attestation migration; caller-only checks can explicitly use online verification."
  "2026-10-19T16:59:35.372Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm coverage pass: 1,358 tests, 1,356 passed, two existing opt-in real-data fleet skips, zero failures/cancellations/TODOs; all 30 measured source files reach 100% statements/branches/functions/lines at unchanged per-file thresholds. actionlint v1.7.12 passes all seven repository workflows plus the caller template with only the pre-existing documented job.workflow_sha schema exception. Package dry-run confirms both source and compiled canonical release metadata are shipped. Required isolated npm and Bun release gates are still running."
  "2026-10-19T17:04:04.514Z",codex-agent,"Both required gates passed with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check. Each: 1,358 tests, 1,356 passed, two pre-existing opt-in fleet skips, zero failures/cancellations/TODOs; 30 measured source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Duplication 0/27,512 lines across 81 sources; 252 documented declarations; zero production vulnerabilities. Package dry-run, changelog/date, attestation and lifecycle checks pass. All eight actionlint inputs pass with the existing documented analyzer exception. No outside-diff findings, review replies/resolutions, bot mentions, merges or releases. Offline snapshot freshness and live release acceptance remain documented migration prerequisites."
  "2026-10-19T18:52:56.791Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: read all three unresolved review threads and confirmed the snapshot freshness gap and untracked release output gap at f5e3a08. Plan: online canonical tag provenance by default for caller policy and attestation, explicit unverified-offline deferral for absent snapshot pins, canonical fork refusal, and tracked/untracked release staging plus a project-wide pack guard. Add behavioral regressions and isolated revert proofs, then unchanged npm/Bun coverage gates and actionlint. No thread replies or resolutions, merges, tags, releases, consumer edits or external deployments."
  "2026-10-19T18:57:16.230Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 implementation: caller CLI, policy and canonical attestation now try canonical tag refs online by default. gh falls back to the public matching-refs API with GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN or anonymous reads; the bundled snapshot is used only if both transports fail. Missing snapshot tags return unverified-offline, never approval; strict policy and attestation defer without a hard failure. Known-tag mismatches and fork-only pins remain refused. The release staging loop includes nonignored untracked outputs and deletions; the pack guard checks the whole package. Tests cover newest pins, transport fallback, offline deferral, adjacent unsafe publishers, and root/nested staging with spaces and first-time files."
  "2026-10-19T18:58:07.241Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 revert proofs: six isolated behavioral reverts each produced 0 pass and 1 fail: default online tag resolution, offline deferral, the policy path reverting to the snapshot, attestation delegation reverting to the snapshot, untracked staging reverting to git diff, and the pack guard reverting to src-only. Sources were restored after each proof; regressions import edited TypeScript or execute edited YAML directly, so no stale dist is involved. Restored focused tests: 24/24 pass, zero skips. All four linked PM test commands pass. PM test reports evidence_recording=tracking_disabled under the existing project policy, so the outcome is recorded in this comment without changing settings."
  "2026-10-19T19:09:35.281Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final gates pass: env HOME=<isolated> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and the equivalent bun run release:check both exit 0. Each reports 1,363 tests: 1,361 passed, two pre-existing opt-in real-data fleet skips, zero failures/cancellations/TODOs. All 30 measured source files achieve 100% statements/branches/functions/lines at unchanged per-file thresholds. Duplication is 0/27,767 lines across 82 sources; 254 declarations pass docstrings; production audit finds zero vulnerabilities. Package dry-run, changelog/date, attestation and lifecycle checks pass. actionlint v1.7.12 passes all seven workflows and the caller template with only the existing workflow_sha analyzer exception. The live canonical API returns 54 release tags, verifies the current pin and refuses the synthetic fork-only SHA. Compiled Node and Bun APIs each pass all three provenance outcomes. PM history remains append-only and added content passes privacy checks. Scope remains source verification; two opt-in fleet checks and live trusted publication are not claimed as acceptance. Review threads remain untouched; no bot mentions, merges, tags, releases, consumer edits or deployments."
  "2026-10-19T20:10:36.036Z",pi-agent,"Review round: fetched all 8 PR review threads; 7 resolved, 1 unresolved (CodeRabbit, index.ts release-caller policy check): canonical release tags are fetched online once per repo because runPolicyCheck calls inspectReleaseCaller without a resolver, and PM_OPS_OFFLINE is ignored there. Verified valid against current code. Also checked the latest CodeRabbit review body: no Outside-diff-range findings. Plan: create a per-policy-run cached tag resolver in the policy path that skips the network when offline and reuses the bundled snapshot fallback; regression tests assert the fetch happens exactly once per run across multiple repos and that PM_OPS_OFFLINE=1 makes zero network calls."
  "2026-10-19T20:14:19.717Z",pi-agent,"Fixed the unresolved review thread: runPolicy now builds one canonical release tag resolver per policy run (createCanonicalTagResolver) and passes it to every release-caller check, so the canonical tag refs are fetched at most once per run instead of once per repository. The resolver throws while PM_OPS_OFFLINE is set, so the release-caller policy check falls back to the bundled release-metadata snapshot exactly like any other unavailable online evidence, and makes zero network calls offline. Revert proof (behavioural): with only the index.ts wiring reverted (caller check back to inspectReleaseCaller without a resolver, no shared resolver), both new regression tests fail - 'ops policy resolves canonical release tags once per policy run' sees two gh tag-refs calls for two repos instead of one, and 'ops policy makes no canonical tag network calls while offline' records a gh call under PM_OPS_OFFLINE=1. With the fix restored both pass."
  "2026-10-19T20:35:29.493Z",pi-agent,"Review round complete. Gates at unchanged thresholds: npm run release:check exit 0 (typecheck, lint, duplication, docstring, coverage gate with full test matrix: 1363 tests pass, 0 fail, audit:prod, pack:dry-run 77 files, changelog:check, release verifies) and bun run release:check exit 0 (same chain, 1363 pass, 0 fail). No merge of origin/main was needed (branch already contains main), no pending merge receipts, no history edits. Changes: index.ts builds one canonical release tag resolver per policy run and honors PM_OPS_OFFLINE; test/ops.test.ts adds two regression tests with behavioural revert proof recorded above. Pre-existing health warnings (global extension version skew, .gitattributes merge-fence drift identical to main) are environmental and unrelated; CI is green on the current head with the same state."
  "2026-10-19T20:40:11.769Z",pi-agent,"Pushed head 371280d (branch feat/reusable-daily-release): CI green on all checks (test matrices for Node 22/26, windows-consumers 22/26, CodeQL). The unresolved review thread fix and both regression tests are in the pushed head; no threads replied to or resolved, no bots mentioned, no merge or release performed."
  "2026-10-19T22:13:45.023Z",pi-agent,"Review round: verified the three unresolved PR review threads against the current head; no Outside-diff-range findings in the latest bot review. All three are valid and fixed: (1) default canonical-tag resolver ignores PM_OPS_OFFLINE in the attestation and CLI paths (release-caller.ts); (2) the CLI online parameter/flag does not change behavior (scripts/release-caller.ts); (3) an unsupported validation-timing claim in the Rust guidance (docs/reusable-release.md)."
  "2026-10-19T22:13:53.408Z",pi-agent,"Fix 1 (default resolver + offline): new exported isPmOpsOffline() and defaultCanonicalTagResolver() in release-caller.ts; inspectReleaseCaller now defaults to that resolver, so PM_OPS_OFFLINE defers online provenance identically in the policy run, the attestation audit and the CLI. index.ts reuses isPmOpsOffline() for its shared offline check instead of a private env comparison."
  "2026-10-19T22:13:57.517Z",pi-agent,"Fix 2 (dead online flag): scripts/release-caller.ts runReleaseCaller drops the unused online parameter and always uses the shared default resolver; the CLI entry no longer parses or filters --online. Offline CLI mode now comes from PM_OPS_OFFLINE. Fix 3 (docs): the Rust guidance no longer claims GitHub validates nested permissions before conditional jobs run; it states the caller template grants issues: write up front to meet the caller-permission ceiling for the nested alert job, since a called workflow can keep or reduce the caller's permissions."
  "2026-10-19T22:14:07.018Z",pi-agent,"Revert proofs (behavioral, fix reverted and only the new regressions re-run): reverting the default-resolver fix alone (inspectReleaseCaller back to fetchCanonicalReleaseTags as the default) fails the two new PM_OPS_OFFLINE tests ('PM_OPS_OFFLINE defers the shared default resolver in the checker and CLI without fetching' and 'PM_OPS_OFFLINE defers the attestation audit's default resolver instead of verifying against the network'): both return verified/recognized against the live fixture instead of unverified-offline. Reverting only the online-flag removal fails the CLI assertion 'the removed --online flag must no longer be filtered out of the path argument' (the flag is filtered again, so no ENOENT is raised). The docs fix is prose-only; the existing test 'caller requires the alert job issues-write permission even without an alert input' pins the issues: write grant the corrected sentence describes."
  "2026-10-19T23:08:08.392Z",pi-agent,"Review round complete and pushed. All three previously unresolved review threads are fixed in one commit with the tracker records: the default canonical-tag resolver defers under PM_OPS_OFFLINE for the checker, attestation audit and CLI alike (index.ts reuses the shared offline check); the behavior-neutral online parameter and --online flag are gone (offline CLI mode is now PM_OPS_OFFLINE); the Rust permissions guidance states the caller-permission ceiling without the unsupported validation-timing claim. Two behavioral regressions added: 'PM_OPS_OFFLINE defers the shared default resolver in the checker and CLI without fetching' (test/release-caller.test.ts) and 'PM_OPS_OFFLINE defers the attestation audit's default resolver instead of verifying against the network' (test/release-caller-attestation.test.ts). Both fail when only the respective fix is reverted; reverting the resolver default returns verified/recognized against the live fixture, reverting the flag removal filters --online again so the ENOENT assertion fails. Docs fix is prose-only and pinned by the existing issues-write permission test."
  "2026-10-19T23:08:11.831Z",pi-agent,"Gates at unchanged thresholds after the fixes: npm run release:check pass (node --test test/*.test.ts: 1367 tests, 1365 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped; coverage-gate 30 source files, thresholds met, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; duplication-gate 0% duplicated lines 0/27968, 0 clone pairs, threshold 0%; docstring-gate 30 files, 255 declarations; pack:dry-run 233.4 kB, 77 files; changelog:check, verify:release-changelog-date, verify:release-publish-attestation and verify:lifecycle-policy all pass). bun run release:check pass with the same counts (1367 tests, 1365 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped; all sub-gates green). No merge was needed: the PR head already contained main, so no merge receipts were involved."
