  "2026-10-20T01:18:54.607Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M6uKap3 fixed: preparation now selects the caller or release-tool fallback pm-cli specifier into cli_version, validates it against the same exact-version grammar as verify_bun, and refuses invalid pins before npm pack or handoff outputs. Fallback require now reads PM_OPS_TOOLS from the environment, avoiding source interpolation for paths containing apostrophes. Actual workflow-shell regression covers 14 caller/fallback fixtures, root/nested projects, exact versions and numeric suffixes, ranges/tags/workspace specs/newlines/missing fallback; valid cases produce real npm tarballs and Git bundles. Behavioral revert proof command: node --test --test-name-pattern='pack validates caller and fallback CLI pins' test/daily-release-workflow.test.ts. Reverting only the pin-validation guard exits 1 (0 pass, 1 fail), accepting ^2026.8.20 incorrectly; independently reverting only the environment-based fallback require exits 1 (0 pass, 1 fail) on the apostrophe fixture. Both implementations restored: 1 pass, 0 fail. Full focused file and pinned pm linked runner: 11 pass, 0 fail, 0 skip. TypeScript test build, lint and zero-duplication checks pass."
